  "preamble": "Stopping and devoicing of the voiced dental fricative [ð] to [t]. Proto-Uralic *δ (written *d in some recent sources) became *t in Proto-Finnic while Mordvinic and Mari kept a voiced reflex: *kuδa- 'weave' > Finnish kutoa, *paδɜ 'dam' > pato. Independently, Proto-Chukotko-Kamchatkan *ð became t in Alutor, where Chukchi has r and Itelmen z or l.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Stopping, Fortition, Devoicing",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Finnish",
      "languageFamily": "Finnic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Uralic *kuδa- 'to weave, spin'",
          "to": "Proto-Finnic *kutodak > Finnish kutoa",
          "note": "Erzya and Moksha кодамс (kodams) and Proto-Samic *koδētēk keep a voiced reflex."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Uralic *paδɜ 'dam, weir'",
          "to": "Proto-Finnic *pato > Finnish pato 'dam'",
          "note": "Compare Proto-Samic *puoδō and Hungarian fal 'wall'."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Uralic *piδe 'tall'",
          "to": "Proto-Finnic *pitkä > Finnish pitkä 'long'",
          "note": "Derived with a suffix; Hungarian fel 'up' is the cognate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Alutor",
      "languageFamily": "Chukotko-Kamchatkan",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Chukotko-Kamchatkan *ðəlɣə 'finger'",
          "to": "тылгылӈын təlɣəlŋən",
          "note": "Compare Chukchi рылгылгын rəlɣəlɣən with r."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Chukotko-Kamchatkan *eðɣə- 'bright'",
          "to": "этгыэтг etɣəetɣ 'light'",
          "note": "Compare Chukchi эргылъын erɣəlʔən."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Chukotko-Kamchatkan *kəð 'you'",
          "to": "гытты ɣəttə",
          "note": "Compare Itelmen кәзза kəzza."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
